# Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request".
@identity = http://localhost:5077

### Health (no token needed) - should say Healthy
GET {{identity}}/health

### 1) Login as receptionist DN10110 (Devendra N, Swetha). Demo password: demo123
# @name login
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "DN10110", "password": "demo123" }

### 2) Who am I (user, hospital, roles, permissions, licensed modules)
GET {{identity}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3) New access token using the refresh cookie set by login
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/refresh

### 4) Sign out (cancels the refresh cookie)
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/logout

### Wrong password -> 400 "Invalid username or password." (5 in a row locks the account for 15 min)
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "DN10110", "password": "wrong" }

### Other demo logins: PS10210 (admin, Swetha), SR10310 (doctor), MS10410 (Dr. Meera Shah), HA10120 (Green Valley)
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "PS10210", "password": "demo123" }

### Public keys other APIs use to check tokens (RS256). Shows "kty": "RSA" and a "kid"; never a private key.
GET {{identity}}/.well-known/jwks.json
